Relevant columns and their potential usage for the requested CNV‑summary task  
(project TCGA‑BRCA, overlap‑weighted copy‑number, frequency of CNV classes):

• "project_short_name": filter rows that belong to breast cancer (“TCGA‑BRCA”).  
• "case_barcode": unique patient / case identifier; used for per‑case statistics.  
• "sample_barcode": tumour/normal sample identifier; choose one (or aggregate many) per case.  
• "aliquot_barcode": aliquot identifier; marks technical replicates of a sample.  
• "chromosome": needed to match genomic intervals to cytobands.  
• "start_pos", "end_pos": define the genomic interval of the CN segment; used for interval overlap with each cytoband.  
• "num_probes": option to weigh segments by probe count or quality filters.  
• "segment_mean": log2(CN/2); used to back‑calculate raw copy number (CN ≈ 2*2^segment_mean), then round/classify.  
• "case_gdc_id", "sample_gdc_id", "aliquot_gdc_id", "file_gdc_id": inner‑join keys if other GDC tables are added; can be used to limit to Release 23 files (not shown here).  

Typical filter / join conditions you may need:  
• WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'  
• AND "file_gdc_id" ILIKE '%release23%'   -- when a release‑tag exists in the file path/ID  
• Chromosome filter: WHERE "chromosome" IN ('chr1','chr2', …, 'chrX')  
• Interval overlap pseudo‑condition when a cytoband table is available:  
  WHERE t."chromosome" = c."chromosome"  
        AND t."start_pos" <= c."end_pos"  
        AND t."end_pos"   >= c."start_pos"  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20) that progressively illustrate how to look at values in the COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED table.  
Replace DATABASE, SCHEMA, and TABLE names exactly as they exist:  
TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0.COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED

```sql
-- 1. Description: show the list of unique TCGA projects contained in the CN‑segment table
SELECT DISTINCT "project_short_name"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: inspect 20 random breast‑cancer (TCGA‑BRCA) CN segments
SELECT *
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: verify the chromosome label formatting seen in TCGA‑BRCA rows
SELECT DISTINCT "chromosome"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: quick view of segment_mean distribution (rounded) for BRCA
SELECT ROUND("segment_mean", 2) AS "segment_mean_rounded",
       COUNT(*) AS "n_segments"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY ROUND("segment_mean", 2)
ORDER BY "n_segments" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: list one sample’s (first alphabetically) segments ordered along the genome
SELECT "chromosome", "start_pos", "end_pos", "segment_mean"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
  AND "sample_barcode" = (
        SELECT MIN("sample_barcode")
        FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
        WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
      )
ORDER BY "chromosome", "start_pos"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: aggregate average log2‑ratio per case and chromosome
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       AVG("segment_mean") AS "avg_segment_mean"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"
ORDER BY "case_barcode", "chromosome"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: convert segment_mean to estimated absolute copy number per segment
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) AS "estimated_CN"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: classify each segment into CNV type using the rounded copy number
SELECT "case_barcode",
       "chromosome",
       "start_pos",
       "end_pos",
       ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean"))        AS "rounded_CN",
       CASE
            WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 0 THEN 'homozygous_deletion'
            WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 1 THEN 'heterozygous_deletion'
            WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 2 THEN 'diploid'
            WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 3 THEN 'gain'
            WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean"))  > 3 THEN 'amplification'
       END                                          AS "CNV_class"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: per case, compute the fraction of segments that are amplifications
SELECT "case_barcode",
       100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) > 3 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
/ NULLIF(COUNT(*),0) AS "pct_amplified_segments"
FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
GROUP BY "case_barcode"
ORDER BY "pct_amplified_segments" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: chromosome‑level CNV class frequency across ALL TCGA‑BRCA segments
SELECT "chromosome",
       "CNV_class",
       COUNT(*) AS "n_segments"
FROM (
      SELECT "chromosome",
             CASE
                  WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 0 THEN 'homozygous_deletion'
                  WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 1 THEN 'heterozygous_deletion'
                  WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 2 THEN 'diploid'
                  WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean")) = 3 THEN 'gain'
                  WHEN ROUND(2 * POWER(2, "segment_mean"))  > 3 THEN 'amplification'
             END AS "CNV_class"
      FROM "TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."TCGA_HG38_DATA_V0"."COPY_NUMBER_SEGMENT_MASKED"
      WHERE "project_short_name" = 'TCGA-BRCA'
) t
GROUP BY "chromosome", "CNV_class"
ORDER BY "chromosome", "n_segments" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

